Now code:

```python
class Solution:
    def largestPower(self, nums: list[int]) -> list[int]:
        nums.sort(reverse=True)
        n = len(nums)
        power = [0] * 15
        for k in range(14, -1, -1):  # k from 14 (MSB) down to 0 (LSB)
            # find first index where bit k is not set
            idx = 0
            mask = 1 << k
            while idx < n and (nums[idx] & mask) != 0:
                idx += 1
            # idx is first index without bit k, so number of elements with prefix all bit k set is idx
            power[14 - k] = idx
        return power
```

